      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Fix Codex fork identity and cache invalidation",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- prefer `session_meta.payload.id` as the canonical Codex leaf-session identifier before parent-oriented `session_id` aliases\n- persist the parent-session file fingerprint used for a fork baseline and invalidate a warm child cache entry whenever that parent appears or changes\n- regenerate the Codex parser hash and add cold-scan plus warm-cache regression coverage\n\n## Why\n\nNewer Codex subagent logs can contain a unique child ID in `payload.id` while `payload.session_id` and `payload.forked_from_id` both point to the parent. Preferring `session_id` aliases multiple child files to the same parent identity.\n\nThere is also a separate warm-cache dependency problem: fork accounting depends on the parent snapshot at the fork timestamp, but cache freshness previously tracked only the child file. If the parent file was missing, discovered later, or appended after the child was cached, the stale child total could continue to include inherited usage.\n\nThis complements the existing fork-baseline and intra-file containment work by fixing cross-file identity and cache dependency invalidation. Refs #2037.\n\n## Redacted runtime proof\n\nThe same frozen 1,692-file Codex corpus was scanned with fresh isolated caches:\n\n| Variant | Total tokens | Unknown model |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| current `main` (`c852c135`) | 705,781,187 | 27,654,293 |\n| this PR (`7b802644`) | 394,500,055 | 0 |\n\nA separate affected corpus was then scanned once from a cold cache and twice through the unchanged warm cache:\n\n| Scan | Total tokens | `gpt-5.6-sol` | `gpt-5.6-terra` | Unknown model |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| cold | 516,961,407 | 435,578,117 | 81,383,290 | 0 |\n| warm 1 | 516,961,407 | 435,578,117 | 81,383,290 | 0 |\n| warm 2 | 516,961,407 | 435,578,117 | 81,383,290 | 0 |\n\nOnly aggregate token and model totals are included. Paths, session IDs, project names, account data, and other identifying metadata are omitted.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `swift test --filter 'CostUsageScannerBreakdownTests|CostUsageCacheTests'` — 89 tests passed\n- `make check` — passed\n- `./Scripts/compile_and_run.sh` — passed; release app built, signed, and launched\n- GitHub macOS test shards, lint, aggregate gate, and Linux ARM64 build — passed\n- Linux x64 reached an unrelated existing `PlatformGatingTests.claudeAutoPipeline_skipsUnsupportedWebAndUsesCLI` failure; the same PR passed the Linux ARM64 matrix and changes no Claude platform-gating code\n- local `make test` also reached two unrelated `AdaptiveRefreshTimerTests` timing failures that reproduce in isolation; no timer code is changed here\n",
        "branch": "agent/fix-codex-fork-cache-baselines",
